 caption←folder GetCommitCaption hash;rc;msg;buff
⍝ Returns a description of `hash`: the short hash, the commit date and the subject.\\
⍝ Suitable both as a title in a comparison utility and for telling the user which
⍝ commit is actually processed.\\
⍝ A dot (".") stands for the working area.
 :If (,'.')≡,hash
     caption←'Working area'
 :Else
     (rc msg buff)←folder RunGitCommand'show -q --date=short --format="%h⍙%cd⍙%s" ',hash
     msg Assert 0=rc
     caption←'⍙'⎕R'  '⊢⊃buff  ⍝ Rather than blanks in the format string; see GetLogFormat for why
 :EndIf
⍝Done
